### Storyboard edit: register CustomViewController

File: `frontend/ios/App/App/Base.lproj/Main.storyboard`

This file is generated by `npx cap add ios` and references the default
`CAPBridgeViewController`. We need it to instantiate our subclass
`CustomViewController` instead — that's how the WKWebView config override
takes effect.

Find this line (exact attributes will vary slightly; the key is the
customClass + customModule pair):

    customClass="CAPBridgeViewController" customModule="Capacitor"

Replace with:

    customClass="CustomViewController" customModule="App"

Notes:
- `customModule` must be `App` (the Xcode target name), not `Capacitor`,
  because the subclass lives in the App target's source files.
- The class name in the storyboard MUST match the Swift class name
  exactly. Mismatch causes a startup crash:
    "Unknown class CustomViewController in Interface Builder file"
